\subsubsection*{B. Project leaders}
Here the records specify objectives for each career category. Status-quo counts
and percentages are calculated from the |gender|, |position|, and funding-period
membership of the |person| records shown in
Section~\ref{sec:manual-consortium-tables}. Only proposals with
|fundingPeriodNumeral = {3}| show the additional first-funding-period columns,
using membership in period~1. By default, the table shows only female
numbers and percentages. For a third-period proposal, it follows DFG
form~60.200: periods~1 and~2 each have Number/Percentage columns; period~3
has its original objective and current Number/Percentage columns. The
existing |future-objective-percentage-female| field supplies that period~3
objective. Include period~3 membership in the person records to calculate
the proposed leadership composition.

Pass |[all-sexes]| before the table name in \refCom{printTable} to select
the expanded f/m/d comparison. For a third-period proposal, every period includes Number and
Percentage columns for f/m/d, alongside the previous period's objective and
the proposed period's future objective. All percentages use the complete f/m/d population in the
same career category (or across the four categories in the total row).
Do not enter these calculated values again in the objectives database;
include historical PIs with the appropriate |period| membership.

\begin{dispListing}
\printTable{GenderEqualityProjectLeaders}            % default: female-only
\printTable[all-sexes]{GenderEqualityProjectLeaders} % f/m/d for all periods
\end{dispListing}

\begin{docKey}{all-sexes}{\docKeyChoices{true,false}}{initially \texttt{false}}
  A per-table option for \cs{GenderEqualityProjectLeadersTable}. The bare flag
  |[all-sexes]| selects f/m/d counts and percentages, including period~3 in a
  third-period proposal, alongside the previous/future objectives.
  Omit the option (or use |[all-sexes=false]|) for the female-only DFG layout.
  Percentages always use all genders as their denominator. The option affects
  only the current table and does not change subsequent tables or prose commands.
  Use |[database=MyObjectives,all-sexes]| for a custom objectives database;
  the older bare database argument also remains supported.
\end{docKey}

