The staff overview counts requested positions by category and year; salary
percentages affect monetary costs, not the number of positions. This example
uses a separate database, |ManualStaffRequest|, to show precisely these two
records. Pass that database as the leading optional argument. In a proposal,
use |RequestedFunding| for the records and omit the table's optional argument
to collect requests across all projects. Projects without requested positions
remain visible with empty-value markers.

\begin{dfgExample}[label={ex:manual-requested-staff-positions-by-category-and-year},dfg wide,listing above* text]{Requested staff positions by category and year}
\addEntry[funding]{ManualStaffRequest}{
  ref-project-id = {B03},
  funding-type   = {staff},
  category       = {PhD},
  percentage     = {65},
