\paragraph{Bibliography font and entry spacing}
The length \cs{bibitemsep} controls the extra vertical gap between bibliography
entries, independently of the line spacing within an entry. A gap can already
be present without a template override: the alphabetic styles inherit
\cs{itemsep}, which is |4pt plus 2pt minus 1pt| in the default 10\,pt setup.
Other bibliography styles may supply different defaults.

To use footnote-sized text and remove this extra gap, add the following hook
outside \cs{changeSettings} in |preamble/dfg-customization.tex|. The file is
read before \pkg{biblatex}, so its lengths and font command must be changed
after the package has loaded.
\begin{dispListing*}{title={Compact bibliographies through the customization file.}}
\AddToHook{package/biblatex/after}{%
  \renewcommand*{\bibfont}{\normalfont\footnotesize}%
  \setlength{\bibitemsep}{0pt}%
}
\end{dispListing*}
This applies to ordinary \cs{printbibliography} calls and to
\refCom{printProjectBibliography} and \refCom{printFrameBibliography}.
Replace |0pt| with |2pt|, for example, to
keep a small extra gap. The CV publication environment |DFGlist| uses
|nosep| already; to add space there, set |itemsep=2pt| after |nosep| in its
list configuration. There is no \cs{changeSettings} key for entry spacing.

\begin{docKey}{emphasizeAuthors}
